            <ArticleTitle>Prediction of enthalpies of sublimation of high-nitrogen energetic compounds: Modified Politzer model.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>220-228</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1093-3263(16)30343-6</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jmgm.2017.01.013</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In the framework of the Politzer approach, the improved electrostatic potential model for estimating enthalpies of sublimation of nitrogen-rich energetic compounds is proposed on the basis of reliable experimental enthalpies of sublimation for 185 compounds. The accuracy of predicted values is estimated to be within ±20kJ/mol. The model was applied to estimate the solid phase enthalpies of formation of some tetrazole-, tetrazine-, furazan-, and furoxan-based energetic compounds.</AbstractText>
